\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Christ the Lord is risen today;
\par Hallelujah!
\par Sons of men and angels say; 
\par Hallelujah!
\par Raise your joy and triumphs high;
\par Hallelujah!
\par Sing, ye heavens, thou earth, reply;
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Love's redeeming work is done;
\par Hallelujah!
\par Fought the fight, the battle won
\par Hallelujah!
\par Vain the stone, the watch, the seal;
\par Hallelujah!
\par Christ hath burst the gates of hell;
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lives again our glorious King;
\par Hallelujah!
\par Where, O death is now thy sting?
\par Hallelujah!
\par Once He died our souls to save;
\par Hallelujah!
\par Where's thy victory, basting grave?
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Soar we now where Christ hast led,
\par Hallelujah!
\par Following our exalted Head:
\par Hallelujah!
\par Made like Him, like Him we rise;
\par Hallelujah!
\par Ours the cross, the grave, the skies;
\par Hallelujah!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. King of glory! Soul of bliss!
\par Hallelujah!
\par Everlasting life is this,
\par Hallelujah!
\par Thee to know, Thy power to prove,
\par Hallelujah!
\par Thus to sing, and thus to love:
\par Hallelujah!
\par  
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

